---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Us - Dujiangyan Panda Base Independent Travel Guide"
  description="About this independent guide to Dujiangyan Panda Base. Meet our team, learn about our editorial standards, and how we keep our travel information accurate."
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-medium tracking-wide text-accent-600 uppercase mb-3">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-warm-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">
      About This Guide
    </h1>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-6 text-warm-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Dujiangyan Panda Base Guide is an independent travel resource created to help international travelers plan their visit to the Dujiangyan Panda Base near Chengdu, China. We are not affiliated with the official base or any government tourism organization — we are travelers who fell in love with this place and wanted to share what we have learned.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mt-10">Our Story</h2>
      <p>
        We first visited the Dujiangyan Panda Base in 2023 and were struck by how different it was from the more famous Chengdu Research Base. Fewer crowds, a quieter hillside setting, and the chance to volunteer alongside the pandas made it one of the most memorable experiences of our travels in China. When we tried to plan our trip, we found information scattered across forums, outdated blog posts, and Chinese-language booking platforms. This guide is our attempt to put everything in one place, in clear English, for fellow travelers.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mt-10">How We Keep Information Accurate</h2>
      <p>
        Travel information — especially prices, opening hours, and booking procedures — changes. We revisit our content regularly and update it based on:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-sm">
        <li>Direct visits to the base (most recent: early 2026)</li>
        <li>Feedback from readers and past volunteers who share their experiences with us</li>
        <li>Monitoring official channels and authorized travel agency listings for price changes</li>
        <li>Cross-referencing with the latest information from the
          <a href="https://en.djy.gov.cn/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline">Dujiangyan Municipal Government</a> tourism portal
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Every page that contains time-sensitive information (prices, hours, booking details) shows a "Last updated" date at the top. If you notice anything that seems out of date, please let us know — we welcome corrections.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mt-10">Editorial Independence</h2>
      <p>
        This guide is independently produced. We do not accept payment for listings, and we are not affiliated with the official Dujiangyan Panda Base, the Chengdu Research Base of Giant Panda Breeding, or any government tourism body. Our recommendations are based on our own experience and what we believe provides the most useful information for international travelers.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-warm-900 mt-10">Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        Have a question, correction, or a story from your own visit? We would love to hear from you. Reach us at <a href="mailto:hello@dujiangyan-panda-base.com" class="text-accent-600 hover:text-accent-700 underline">hello@dujiangyan-panda-base.com</a>. We typically respond within 2-3 days.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
